WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.450
In the year to June 2023, about 339,000
people moved into England's mostly rural

2
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:08.810
council areas.

3
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:13.390
And 278,400 moved out.

4
00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.510
Officially, in England, rural means
outside any settlement of more than 10,000

5
00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:19.630
people.

6
00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:25.190
In 2024, 17 per cent of England's
people lived in rural settlements.

7
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.910
So what do all these moves
do to England's villages?

8
00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:33.790
In this mission, you'll line up settlements
from city centre to isolated farm,

9
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.230
and map their spheres of influence.

10
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:40.850
Then you'll find out why people move,
and what changes when they arrive.

11
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:44.930
Your mission: decide what all
this moving does to villages.
